cycle. CenturyLink has reviewed the accompanying security advisories and would like to provide the following information:

**CVE-2019-0708 | Remote Desktop Services Remote Code Execution Vulnerability**

A remote code execution vulnerability exists in Remote Desktop Services formerly known as Terminal Services

[CVE-2019-0708](https://portal.msrc.microsoft.com/en-US/security-guidance/advisory/CVE-2019-0708)

[Prevent a worm by updating remote desktop services](https://blogs.technet.microsoft.com/msrc/2019/05/14/prevent-a-worm-by-updating-remote-desktop-services-cve-2019-0708/)

Microsoft has released updates for all affected operating systems, this includes releasing a Windows 2003 specific update, which reinforces the severity of the issue. Windows 2008 and Windows 2008 R2 are also impacted but more modern operating systems are not exposed to the same vulnerability.

**Impact During Maintenance**

During this maintenance window, CenturyLink will install the required Microsoft patch to mitigate the risk, which will involve a reboot of the server operating system. CenturyLink will ensure that the server installs the required patch and is rebooted successfully. Any issues that arise from the maintenance will be managed via the standard Incident Management process.

**Additional Information**

If you have any questions or concerns, please contact your Service Management representative or the service desk for more information @ 

**Global Client Response Center**: 1 888 638 6771 (US) | 00800 7288 4743 or +44 (0)118 322 6100 (UK)
